o's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:24:04-08:00","id":825931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=820536#post820536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been reading <i>all</i> the Mage dev blogs again for the n-th time (agh! need... 2e... now...) and got to the supernal summoning Attainments. I don't know, how exactly will they work in 2e, but they gave me this idea of a mage who falls in love with a Supernal being during their awakening and keeps seeing them anytime the mage activates their Mage Sight (apparently having a Supernal ally you see like this is a Merit in 2e too!), but can't even touch them.<br /> <br /> The relationship would have serious star-crossed lovers undertones and a constant temptation for the mage to repeatedly summon the being fully into reality to experience at least some moments of physical contact. Predictable consequences would probably follow soon after.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another related idea I had is a Goetic Mage, who falls in love/gets obsessed with their demon of Lust. To call it a co-dependent potentially destructive relationship probably doesn't do the situation justice.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if the mage wants the Consilium to recognize the demon as a full member of Pentacle society. Sure, the demon might be pretty intelligent, but, well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:40:13-08:00","id":825936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=825931#post825931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another related idea I had is a Goetic Mage, who falls in love/gets obsessed with their demon of Lust. To call it a co-dependent potentially destructive relationship probably doesn't do the situation justice.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if the mage wants the Consilium to recognize the demon as a full member of Pentacle society. Sure, the demon might be pretty intelligent, but, well...</div> </div> </div> </div>And for weird reasons he call her &quot;A <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Succubus\" target=\"_blank\">Succubus</a>&quot; and says she comes to him in his dreams... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T08:08:25-08:00","id":825994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=825931#post825931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another related idea I had is a Goetic Mage, who falls in love/gets obsessed with their demon of Lust. To call it a co-dependent potentially destructive relationship probably doesn't do the situation justice.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if the mage wants the Consilium to recognize the demon as a full member of Pentacle society. Sure, the demon might be pretty intelligent, but, well...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm fairly certain that wouldn't fly in an Assembly, simply for the reason: how would it affect voting when any competent Mind mage can have all their no-longer invisible friends vote along with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T18:54:42-08:00","id":826459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=825994#post825994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm fairly certain that wouldn't fly in an Assembly, simply for the reason: how would it affect voting when any competent Mind mage can have all their no-longer invisible friends vote along with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? I imagine it would even out fairly quickly, as paths seem fairly evenly spread across the Orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T20:34:52-08:00","id":830759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=823557#post823557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's fine!<br /> <br /> But why are you here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because while I actively dislike romances in RPG, it isn't a excuse to not understand how writing them works and studying them. I need to understand my enemy to get sweet racial enemy crit bonus against it. And, more importantly, I need to have comprehension of it in case if any of my players decides it's what they want in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T21:21:12-07:00","id":1113555,"title":"","content":"Well, here's some visual elements for the characters in this dating sim.*<br /> Vampire would be pretty easy. Pale smooth skin, long straight raven black hair, fancy crimson dress.<br /> Werewolf you need to play into a more tomboy wild girl vibe, shredded punk clothes and so on<br /> Mage you could either go shy nerd or 'OH-HOHOHO~' lady<br /> Promethean gentle giant misunderstood loner would probably be best<br /> Changeling you could do way to many things with, honestly that ones going to be the hardest<br /> Demon would be sexy secret agent character<br /> Geist I would imagine is the more sober and composed loner gal, always with the same half smile on her face<br /> I say, on a year old thread.*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T22:08:51-07:00","id":1113592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1113555#post1113555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, here's some visual elements for the characters in this dating sim.*<br /> Vampire would be pretty easy. Pale smooth skin, long straight raven black hair, fancy crimson dress.<br /> Werewolf you need to play into a more tomboy wild girl vibe, shredded punk clothes and so on<br /> Mage you could either go shy nerd or 'OH-HOHOHO~' lady<br /> Promethean gentle giant misunderstood loner would probably be best<br /> Changeling you could do way to many things with, honestly that ones going to be the hardest<br /> Demon would be sexy secret agent character<br /> Geist I would imagine is the more sober and composed loner gal, always with the same half smile on her face<br /> I say, on a year old thread.*</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose, but those are all a little cliche. Personally, here's what I'd do. I'm just gonna go with whatever gender I happen to choose for each one, so, assume a bi or pan protagonist, I guess?<ul><li>Vampires: A bored smart-ass who happens to be immortal, and has seen so many neonate edgelords that any time he sees a vamp slinking about in black robes quoting Byron or some shit, he feels compelled to scream <b>&quot;CRAAAAAAAAWLING IN MY SKIIIIIIIIN</b>&quot; at the top of his lungs. He wears pretty simple, plain clothes, with maybe a few very small touches of color here or there. Depending how &quot;alt&quot; he is, he might have his hair dyed a dark-ish red.</li> <li>Werewolf: At first glance, maybe kind of a &quot;hippie&quot; chick. Then she takes you out hunting for a weekend and you realize that she's also improbably proficient with a crossbow. She's sweet, she's peaceful, she just broke that guy's arm for grabbing her ass. She is, in a word, &quot;<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/WgJUTRs.gif\" target=\"_blank\">scarousing</a>.&quot;</li> <li>Mage: A hard-core Libertine activist, with a restrictive Seer daddy who's unaware of her Order association. Her route <i>will</i> result in the both of you being arrested at some point. She's pretty rich, but she clearly tries to dress like she's not, to the point that it seems like she's ashamed of her wealth, probably because of how her family came by it. Do not discuss economics with her unless you have studied the hell up.</li> <li>Promethean: Galateid, and absolutely god-damned-drop-dead gorgeous girl. Unfortunately, not everyone recognizes that she <i>is</i> a girl. She's dressed as cutely as possible at all times, partly as a sort of defiance, but mostly because she likes feeling pretty. Her route is arguably the most involved and difficult, due to her pretty justified defensiveness and Disquiet.</li> <li>Changeling: Part of a really, really tight-knit clique, that the protagonist later finds out is also a support group. He dresses really plainly in public or when his parents are around, but in his route, he'll take you with him to a concert, and he will be wearing the most aggressively punk-rock get-up imaginable.</li> <li>Demon: She just really likes dressing up. &quot;Clothes horse&quot; describes him to a tee, and the best way to her heart is to go clothes shopping with him.</li> <li>Geist: The class clown. He pulls pranks that should, quite honestly, kill him. Sometimes he does the whole &quot;wearing black&quot; thing, but even then, he makes it his own. He doesn't ever really have a consistent style, but he just kinda takes whatever doesn't smell too dodgy from his clothes bin and makes it work.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T22:51:30-07:00","id":1113608,"title":"","content":"Well, if this thread is getting revived we might as well include some more potential romances. So, what would the Beast and Deviant paths be like? Clearly we have to have a plain Jane mortal human as one of the paths (whether they're a Hunter or not is up to debate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T23:13:52-07:00","id":1113617,"title":"","content":"Hunters would have to be absolutely separate. Probably the stand-offish &quot;bad path&quot; that reveals the hunter character is just a misunderstood loner in the school and just wants to do some good, but can't get out of the shadow of their &quot;older siblings&quot; (conspiracy-level hunters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T04:37:07-07:00","id":1113679,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on Protagonist:<br /> <br /> One Possiblity is a normal Mortal who though some accident or other manages to lose all forms of &quot;Control&quot; upon them.. they can see each person for what they really are and accept them for it. (Based loosely on the Protagonist from Saya no Uta.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank"