sted at some point. She's pretty rich, but she clearly tries to dress like she's not, to the point that it seems like she's ashamed of her wealth, probably because of how her family came by it. Do not discuss economics with her unless you have studied the hell up.</li> <li>Promethean: Galateid, and absolutely god-damned-drop-dead gorgeous girl. Unfortunately, not everyone recognizes that she <i>is</i> a girl. She's dressed as cutely as possible at all times, partly as a sort of defiance, but mostly because she likes feeling pretty. Her route is arguably the most involved and difficult, due to her pretty justified defensiveness and Disquiet.</li> <li>Changeling: Part of a really, really tight-knit clique, that the protagonist later finds out is also a support group. He dresses really plainly in public or when his parents are around, but in his route, he'll take you with him to a concert, and he will be wearing the most aggressively punk-rock get-up imaginable.</li> <li>Demon: She just really likes dressing up. &quot;Clothes horse&quot; describes him to a tee, and the best way to her heart is to go clothes shopping with him.</li> <li>Geist: The class clown. He pulls pranks that should, quite honestly, kill him. Sometimes he does the whole &quot;wearing black&quot; thing, but even then, he makes it his own. He doesn't ever really have a consistent style, but he just kinda takes whatever doesn't smell too dodgy from his clothes bin and makes it work.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about Beasts? <br /> I see tentacles! Lots and lots of tentacles!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T08:06:08-07:00","id":1113735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1113721#post1113721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What about Beasts?<br /> I see tentacles! Lots and lots of tentacles!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Consentacles is bestacles!<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, we haven't touched on the Deviant. I'm thinking the non-neutral childhood friend who after &quot;the accident&quot; has started to totally define themselves around protecting you. Bad route is getting into a codependent relationship. Good route is helping them find some cause to define themselves around instead and setting them free. On looks though, I got nothing. Though perhaps take cues from Katawa Shoujo characters<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1113679#post1113679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on Protagonist:<br /> <br /> One Possiblity is a normal Mortal who though some accident or other manages to lose all forms of &quot;Control&quot; upon them.. they can see each person for what they really are and accept them for it. (Based loosely on the Protagonist from Saya no Uta.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That could end reeeeeeally badly if its anything like Saya no Uta. <br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> *evil smile* I love it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-09-2017, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:48:28-07:00","id":1113866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1113721#post1113721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What about Beasts?<br /> I see tentacles! Lots and lots of tentacles!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDefinitely for a Makara in a generic city. Could also go with a dom dragon girl","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T23:08:09-07:00","id":1114453,"title":"","content":"I think there should be a dating sim for each splat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T02:18:22-07:00","id":1114489,"title":"","content":"Ok, I have these ideas for beast:<br /> Anakim &quot;Tall Girl&quot; Tsundere, who can give you a &quot;BAKA!!!!!-slap&quot; so hard, it spins your head around. She is a bit bossy with her friends and is number one in the track-team. Usually wears some kind of sporty clothes. Has a kind side, but if you get too close too fast, she'll twist your arm onto your back in no time<br /> <br /> Marakan &quot;Weird Chick&quot;. She is shy and usually seems mentally absent. Spends most of the time in the swimming club or on the library computers. Always wears some kind of seashell pendant, otherwise dresses very bland. Get's really agitated when someone eats calamari. And once you get closer to her TENTACLES! TENTACLES EVERYWHERE! (Or suction cups if you're into that too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T11:04:00-07:00","id":1114675,"title":"","content":"For the hunters, I'll do some of the Conspiracies:<br /> <br /> Aigis Kai Doru: A nerdy, bookish girl who hides behind the mask of an amoral, almost mechanical killer of monsters. In reality, the only time we see her &quot;game face&quot; is when she's pursuing monsters she knows are completely inhuman; she's secretly a pacifist who distrusts her superiors. Her ending involves her either killing you in the bed after being bullied into it (and starting a vengeful rebellion against the AKD) or quitting and provoking a split in the Guardians between traditionalists and reformists who are sick of being dragged around by a myth that their information tells them isn't even true.<br /> <br /> Cheiron Group: The &quot;rich snobby genius&quot; character. He was volunteered for treatment in intelligence-increasing Thaumatech when he was young, and this has led him to be a prodigy and utterly ruthless businessman. Secretly, he's utterly miserable; he isn't sure if he's human, and he displays a far nicer side to his personality once he becomes aware you're dating (after bluntly asking why you're attracted to him when it's clear he's bad news and probably will hurt you-the answer that solidifies a date is &quot;Because you're afraid of being bad news&quot;).<br /> <br /> Knights of St. Adrian: Your typical Lad-ette; female and proud of it, but a tomboy's tomboy with her motorcycle and love of big explosions. Her real arc starts up, however, when she meets the demon-and realizes that the Unchained does not match her mental image of the Infernal at all, and leading her to realize who and what she's working for. She ends up shutting herself away in a house for a while to stew in self-loathing and guilt unless you coax her out-and convince her not to go out in a blaze of glory, taking a large amount of Infrastructure with her (mostly by convincing her it'd be more effective to blow it up steathily and safely).<br /> <br /> Merrick Institute: The emo kid. Mostly it's an affectation, but he's genuinely depressed after they experimented on him and stole his life. He doesn't hate Beasts. being a friend of one of the above, and probably one of the nicest LIs. Also the one most loyal to his Conspiracy as a whole.<br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum: You guessed it, she's the nun. A very unhappy nun who has lost any respect she had for the Church. She's the most blatantly angry at the core of her Conspiracy, having discovered what Baudolino was and that he hunts vampires to maintain his immortality, after she lost several loved ones to sacrificing themselves for the Shadow Congregation. She is in a very dark place when you meet her, all hiding it under a placid smile; she actually ends up propositioning you (actually earlier if you're a woman) soon after you realize you're no friend of the Inquisition, mostly because she's spiting everything and everyone connected with the Malleus. The darkest LI, but there's two happy endings with her-one where she finally works up the will to be honest about her broken faith and why, and another where she learns who Baudolino is and comes to forgive him-though she's still excommunicated, she retains her Benedictions in that case.<br /> <br /> VASCU: A hunky cop with psychic powers. There's really not much more to explain characterization-wise, he's a typical Noir-ish detective. The other bisexual hunter LI, gets involved due to pursuing the main antagonist.<br /> <br /> The Main Antagonist: A Legend Slasher who went psycho after hunters killed her mage wife. She's &quot;the Hunter of Hunters&quot;, someone called to hurt the Vigil back. She is not a good person; while she technically has a route in the hunter-focused game, she's just using you to get close to her targets (as shown by her &quot;attraction&quot; to males; she loves you not at all, it's not hard to fake sexuality). At best, her ending has her grow fond of you...so she takes your heart, literally, and makes your soul into her pet. It's made quite clear this is even worse than her murdering you, because she uses you as a target of her aggression.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The plot for the hunter-focused game, if they have their own, revolves around the theme of revenge; all the LIs have people they hate for understandable reasons, with their hatred consuming them to varied degrees. The bad endings of each route involve the LI becoming an Avenger for some reason or another (naturally, the antagonist has been consumed a long time ago-there's no way to save her). The last scenes all involve them planning their first murder and discovering their MO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-13-2017, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T21:37:17-07:00","id":1114910,"title":"","content":"Aren't there also Japanese Hunter Compacts/Conspiracies we need to consider? I mean, it's probably important given the dating sim's popularity in Japan.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, minor supernaturals should probably get love.<br /> <br /> <br /> An Immortal I imagine is a guy who thinks he's simply too old for love... or too young, and involves reincarnation shenanigans of which you are a part of, though depending on immortality, may not. I imagine he'd be somewhat jaded and bored. Though not a hedonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T19:26:30-07:00","id":1115339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1113592#post1113592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose, but those are all a little cliche. Personally, here's what I'd do. I'm just gonna go with whatever gender I happen to choose for each one, so, assume a bi or pan protagonist, I guess?<ul><li>Vampires: A bored smart-ass who happens to be immortal, and has seen so many neonate edgelords that any time he sees a vamp slinking about in black robes quoting Byron or some shit, he feels compelled to scream <b>&quot;CRAAAAAAAAWLING IN MY SKIIIIIIIIN</b>&quot; at the top of his lungs. He wears pretty simple, plain clothes, with maybe a few very small touches of color here or there. Depending how &quot;alt&quot; he is, he might have his hair dyed a dark-ish red.</li> <li>Werewolf: At first glance, maybe kind of a &quot;hippie&quot; chick. Then she takes you out hunting for a weekend and you realize that she's also improbably proficient with a crossbow. She's sweet, she's peaceful, she just broke that guy's arm for grabbing her ass. She is, in a word, &quot;<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/WgJUTRs.gif\" target=\"_blank\">scarousing</a>.&quot;</li> <li>Mage: A hard-core Libertine activist, with a restrictive Seer daddy who's unaware of her Order association. Her route <i>will</i> result in the both of you being arrested at some point. She's pretty rich, but she clearly tries to dress like she's not, to the point that it seems like she's ashamed of her wealth, probably because of how her family came by it. Do not discuss economics with her unless you have studied the hell up.</li> <li>Promethean: Galateid, and absolutely god-damned-drop-dead gorgeous girl. Unfortunately, not everyone recognizes that she <i>is</i> a girl. She's dressed as cutely as possible at all times, partly as a sort of defiance, but mostly because she likes feeling pretty. Her route is arguably the most involved and difficult, due to her pretty justified defensiveness and Disquiet.</li> <li>Changeling: Part of a really, really tight-knit clique, that the protagonist later finds out is also a support group. He dresses really plainly in public or when his parents are around, but in his route, he'll take you with him to a concert, and he will be wearing the most aggressively punk-rock get-up imaginable.</li> <li>Demon: She just really likes dressing up. &quot;Clothes horse&quot; describes him to a tee, and the best way to her heart is to go clothes shopping with him.</li> <li>Geist: The class clown. He pulls pranks that should, quite honestly, kill him. Sometimes he does the whole &quot;wearing black&quot; thing, but even then, he makes it his own. He doesn't ever really have a consistent style, but he just kinda takes whatever doesn't smell too dodgy from his clothes bin and makes it work.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Hah! I gotta admit, those sound good. Even the ladies. But somehow that self ironic and sardonic vampire sounds like the only kind of datable vampire.<br /> <br /> More interesting is if this dating sim included some of the mechanics of the monster for each dating target. If you don't give the vampire blood, does your sweet lover get more tense and angry? Does your mummy get younger and prettier every scene? When dating s changeling, since you can't see their fae me in as a human, how much of a ''good day'' versus ''bad day'' is it in terms of their clarity?<br /> <br /> As for CofD romance, my favorite it still Mummy. Its the only time I didn't feel ironic for pulling in that C\u00e9line Dion song from Titanic. A mummy lover is like the Fountain, The Fault in Our Stars, Love Story, the Notebook...... plus plagues and godlike power. My main mummy pc (who isn't a mummy but a reincarnation soul with past life memory) is in love with a former master. That mummy forgot his flexible sexuality, and is obsessing over his two wives--a Deceived and a Shuanksen. The romance is beautiful, tragic, fast, passionate, and doomed. Mummy romance is truly epic.<br /> <br /> Though I will admit that Demon comes in a close second in terms of how intensely cool true love is for them, considering the liar's tongue and poker face. Loving someone enough to given them your secrets, secrets that could kill you, or worse. It somehow makes things feel especially intimate. not sexually so, just... close. personal. In Demon, love is a weakness, a danger, but because of it so sweet. To make a machine feel? To make a being who once held creation itself in his hands submit to you? To find love in Hell? Truly beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:05:03-07:00","id":1115367,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with both Demon and Mummy being pretty cool for romance stories. I had a non-Dating Sim bouncing around in my head about a Mummy in Macedonia during Alexandrian times creating a Sadikh out of their lover and then awakening together throughout the ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:40:41-07:00","id":1115584,"title":"","content":"Actually, Katawa Shoujo has a nice trick-every girl's plot has a driving question at the core.<br /> <br /> That seems like a nice trick for us too. So:<br /> <br /> Vampire: &quot;Can you control your passions?&quot;<br /> <br /> Werewolf: &quot;Can you be relied on?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage: &quot;Will you chose ignorance?&quot;<br /> <br /> Promethean: &quot;Will you always accept a monster?&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;Can you stand another's pain?&quot;<br /> <br /> Demon: &quot;Will you be trustworthy?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T13:43:33-07:00","id":1115656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1115584#post1115584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Katawa Shoujo has a nice trick-every girl's plot has a driving question at the core.<br /> <br /> That seems like a nice trick for us too. So:<br /> <br /> Vampire: &quot;Can you control your passions?&quot;<br /> <br /> Werewolf: &quot;Can you be relied on?&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage: &quot;Will you choose ignorance?&quot;<br /> <br /> Promethean: &quot;Will you always accept a monster?&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling: &quot;Can you stand another's pain?&quot;<br /> <br /> Demon: &quot;Will you be trustworthy?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter: Will you stay as the Vigil makes them unrecognizable?<br /> <br /> Deviant: How do you bond with a broken soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T03:38:28-07:00","id":1115862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1114910#post1114910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Immortal I imagine is a guy who thinks he's simply too old for love... or too young, and involves reincarnation shenanigans of which you are a part of, though depending on immortality, may not. I imagine he'd be somewhat jaded and bored. Though not a hedonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Or if you want a Darker one... who is abit older (Physically) and is getting to know you better... so they can better mimic you once they borrow your body..... Probably a Bad End Route....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T03:41:10-07:00","id":1115863,"title":"","content":"<br /> A fairest changling who's got nothing going for them except their strangely attractive self. They're pushed out of the Faerie nest (cage) into a mean cruel world filled with neutral encounters with interested and engaging and often slightly threatening/scary/weird/gross members of the different splats. (perhaps a little artificially, but what dating sim isn't a little artificial?) The Keeper asserts itself often and unexpectedly, throwing the changeling into the care, or at least an immediate common cause with whatever splat they're current with.<br /> <br /> Relationships evolve as the changeling must lie extravagantly to explain Keeper situation, or tell the truth, or beg or negotiate for help or alliance.. . or run away afterwards.. or whatever the player decides to do. The one thing the player can't really decide to do is be captured by the Keeper again (though even that should be an option.) The splats respond frequently in harem game kind of ways, with an array of personalities that never fully shut out the changeling, but entice different kinds of interactions in a variety of romantic ways and also draw the changeling into learning about each of the splats' strange and secret world that houses its own wonders and dangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-14-2017, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T18:16:00-07:00","id":1116186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=640562#post640562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone is in a nightclub. The main character is ahunter who has to decide to date or kill every other supernatural. Sometimes both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, a/n <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Anita Blake </div></div> </div> </div> rip-off. Gotcha'!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T17:31:15-07:00","id":1116602,"title":"","content":"One point I haven't seen raised yet is the Deava clan bane means you could end up with a lot of power in the relationship making a Deava love intrest very careful to ensure you can be trusted. Are there any other possible love interests that have reason not to trust the protagonist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T22:59:14-07:00","id":1116738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1116602#post1116602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One point I haven't seen raised yet is the Deava clan bane means you could end up with a lot of power in the relationship making a Deava love intrest very careful to ensure you can be trusted. Are there any other possible love interests that have reason not to trust the protagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Galateids and Prometheans in general, due to Disquiet and the risks of their Torment.<br /> <br /> Depending on their Kuruth triggers and the level of danger their Pack might be in if a secret slipped out, Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Beasts need to worry about their prospective lover being either a Hero, or within reach for a Hero to threaten or manipulate.<br /> <br /> Changelings, for the same reason as Beasts, replacing Hero with Huntsman, as well as the possible dangers of Freehold politics.<br /> <br /> Demons for...well, everything. Just, everything, everything, everything.<br /> <br /> Arguably, you could fit it into most every splat. The ChroD world is incredibly paranoid, for good reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T19:55:05-07:00","id":1118035,"title":"","content":"Actually, here's an underpinning plot for the supernatural-focused version;<br /> <br /> Watch SF Debris' review of Kannazuki No Miko, and then twist it so that the fundamentally unhealthy nature of the main romance is the whole point. You come into this setting knowing you're destined to meet someone you loved in a previous life...and then you discover your &quot;soulmate&quot; is a psycho with no capacity to express affection in a healthy way. If you happen to have been playing your cards right, your character discovers that s/he is fated to duel their soulmate to the death as part of this cyclic ritual to keep a gate to the Underworld firmly shut...and reacts with guilty relief, because at this point s/he hates the soulmate's guts. The plot is to use your love for another, unrelated person to break the cycle forever and free you from this endless reincarnating hell.<br /> <br /> For bonus points, the mage brings up that in Theosophy, soul<i>foes</i> exist as well, and it's entirely possible your &quot;soulmate&quot; is actually your eternal nemesis.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's another plan spinning off from this; the kickoff is an amoral entity, maybe the God-Machine, interfering in the ritual to actually <i>upgrade</i> the binding-so long as the door is shut based on the feelings of two people, there are too many possible scenarios where the rite goes awry and the door is busted open. If you go with the idea of the angelic Exposition Fairy, maybe they Fall by dropping the pretext and revealing the G-M's motives in all this because they're sick of lying. The demon, if on his path, then may wonder if the angel Falling was part of its plan...then decides it doesn't matter, because she couldn't live with himself if she knew you were stuck in this unending cycle of misery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-19-2017, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:58:35-07:00","id":1120170,"title":"","content":"Also, secret LIs!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Huntsman: One of the enslaved fae taking after a man-eater like the Jorogumo or the Impundulu; you unlock them by an event where they attack the changeling early in your relationship, but somehow manage to reconnect them and their heart outside of the Hedge, allowing them enough free will to fight back against the Keeper and help you look for their heart. A classical tsundere, hiding their pain behind snark and anger at their situation. A good ending involves you becoming part of Arcadia as another Huntsman-but one that can never be bound by a Keeper. Driving question: &quot;Can you teach a slave to remember freedom?&quot;<br /> <br /> Alchemist: You encounter him lurking around the Promethean eyeing them hungrily. He, however, does not have the heart to be a mad scientist, and is unlocked if you confront him on this and force him to reveal his motives-and acknowledge he's just hurting another for the sake of himself, even if it is for a sympathetic reason. He's by far the most socially awkward LI and not conventionally attractive (he's a tad overweight, though your character thinks he's like a big teddy bear). Driving question: &quot;What are your boundaries?&quot; (Which is a lot creepier than it comes off in practice-it's a reference to his experiments).<br /> <br /> Hero: A wannabe magical girl who's a bit more self-aware than most of her kind. You unlock her by entertaining her when she's stalking the Beast, but in a way that causes her to realize the Beast is not a threat. She's a bit of a bitch, but extremely honorable and fair, and well-aware of when to become sweet; think Weiss from RWBY with a shotgun. Driving question: &quot;What do you most value?&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T19:45:30-07:00","id":1120190,"title":"","content":"And here's some more while I'm here:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Fox Changing Breed: Unlocked by failing the route with the Werewolf at the right point in the right way, where you both decide it's not going to work, so she set you up with a Were-fox packmate, though both of you feel pretty guilty about it. The fundamental question of this route is &quot;When is it okay to love again?&quot;</li> <li>Goetic: He's beauty, grace, and the man of your dreams. Literally. You first meet him in either the Mage or the Beast route, and if you are in the Mage route, you can awaken to Mastigos and call him up again (thus failing the Mage route in the process, since you're dumping your real girlfriend for an imaginary boyfriend). He seems like your pefect match, your rather literal soulmate, but he sometimes seems a little possessive. His fundamental question is &quot;What is the line between love and obsession?&quot;</li> <li>Ghost: This can come up in any route, but is most likely in the Sin-Eater route. The ghost can be of one of the other love interests, if they died at any point, or a new LI unto their own. Either way, the fundamental question is &quot;When is it time to let go?&quot;</li> <li>Angel: If you amicably end the Demon Route (either with a successful romance, or with an amicable split), this unlocks the Angel route upon starting a new game, in which the Angel attempts to get to the Demon through you, hoping the shift in the timeline will go unnoticed by the Demon. Unless the right things happen, she will appear to be a Stigmatic, but if you see through her, you can attempt to free her from the God-Machine (resulting in a Fall), find a loophole in her mission (resulting in an Exile), side with the Demon (whom you may not be romantically entangled with in this timeline!) and kill her, or choose to assist her and get the Demon collected and melted down in the process. The question of this route is &quot;How far will you go for your lover?&quot; If you do everything <i>perfectly</i>, with the Fall or Exile route, you could even manage a poly ending with the Demon and the Exile/other Demon.</li> <li>Nobility: Dummied out in the game's code, if you edit it back in, there's a chance to start this route during that protest that the Mage LI takes you to early on in her route, and he makes you a Sworn later on. His route's main question is &quot;When is it okay to choose yourself over others?&quot;</li> <li>Genius: Also dummied out, you can meet her from the start if you edit her back in. Her primary question is &quot;Is it more important to be right, or just?&quot;</li> <li>The God-Machine: If you manage to get <i>every single other ending</i>, good bad or neutral, for every route, including the hidden and joke endings (Including self-romancing via time shards), and even the dummied-out LIs, then you can start a new game where everything is a little...off. People have imperceptible glitches, the sound hiccups slightly once in a while, and occasionally the wrong backgrounds or people will briefly appear before being replaced with the right one. If you poke at it and question it enough, everything will be laid bare, and you'll realize that everything is one thing: the God-Machine. And it wants to be your boyfr-er, girlfr-uh...Bot-friend? Let's go with that. The fundamental question of this route is &quot;Da fuh?&quot;</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-24-2017, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T21:24:08-07:00","id":1120223,"title":"","content":"Perfect now we have 2 make this game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T21:37:54-07:00","id":1120227,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you couldn't make a text version of it in SCRATCH. Mostly because that removes the need for extensive art, which may make it more likely to be competed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T21:56:18-07:00","id":1120233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwod-as-a-dating-simulator-what-would-it-be-like?p=1120227#post1120227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you couldn't make a text version of it in SCRATCH. Mostly because that removes the need for extensive art, which may make it more likely to be competed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably could. I'd probably use Python or maybe Javascript if it's going to be web-based, but Scratch would probably work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T23:16:31-07:00","id":1120246,"title":"","content":"And if it all gos well we can make a kickstarter maybe probs not but i can dream about it and also who's your fav mines god machine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T21:21:01-07:00","id":1120633,"title":"","content":"If we make a Kickstarter, we'd need to ask for company permission for it. And then have some of us act as writers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T02:21:17-07:00","id":1120707,"title":"","content":"Indeed we should we don't want copyright clams after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:01:22-07:00","id":1120801,"title":"","content":"Who knows, maybe somebody could make a prototype and pitch it to Paradox. It's unlikely, but theoretically possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T07:33:33-07:00","id":1228575,"title":"","content":"Suddenly, I feel need to revive this, both for the Contagion Chronicle giving an internal justification for all the LIs in the same social circle...and because Jackbox Games had the same idea.<br /> <br /> Look up Monster Seeking Monster, and make a typical match a full game plot with the full recognition that kind of social engineering would only happen with horrible people (see: Two-Faced Creep, playable role).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T09:36:26-07:00","id":1228605,"title":"","content":"So... bring on the Demon+Beast Fics (Slash optional)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T12:52:39-07:00","id":1228653,"title":"","content":"It'd say CoD date simulator would be the scariest one this side of Japan, this is a horror game, so your night ending with your date trying to eat you, and not in the fun way, is a distinct possiblity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T13:30:52-07:00","id":1228667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/640173-nsfw-nwo